  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Illinois has $11.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 473,041 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $23.6K. Obligations fell 10.3% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show a peak at $13.6B in FY22 and a decline to $11.1B in FY26 after FY25 obligations of $12.4B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in Illinois, obligating $5.9B so far this fiscal year. Medical, research, and wholesale industries account for much of the spending, led by Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $1.2B and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $1.1B. W S DARLEY & CO leads vendors with $1.5B in obligations, followed by UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC at $1.1B and MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP at $943M. The figures are fiscal year to date and therefore partial totals for FY2026.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did Illinois federal contract spending change across recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Illinois recorded $12B in FY21, $13.6B in FY22, $13B in FY23, $13.4B in FY24, $12.4B in FY25, and $11.1B in FY26 to date. Obligations fell 10.3% year over year into FY26 to date. The FY26 figure is a partial, fiscal year to date total. The sequence shows a peak in FY22 and lower obligations through FY26 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers, industries, and vendors in Illinois federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buying agency with $5.9B in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $1.9B and the Department of Energy at $1.9B. The leading industries are Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $1.2B and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $1.1B. W S DARLEY & CO is the largest vendor with $1.5B, followed by UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC at $1.1B and MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP at $943M."
      }
    ]
  },
